[comment encoding = UTF-8 /]

[**
Module contains queries with a UML data type as receiver.
This includes queries for navigating the data type hierarchy
(supertypes, subtypes), finding properties that use a data type,
and data type classification.

Note: Queries applicable to both classes and data types
are in classifierQuery, since both are subtypes of Classifier.

Related modules:
- classQuery: queries with a UML class as receiver
- classifierQuery: queries with a UML classifier as receiver,
  applicable to both classes and data types
/]
[module dataTypeQuery(
	'http://www.eclipse.org/uml2/5.0.0/UML',
	'http://www.eclipse.org/uml2/5.0.0/Types',
	'http://www.eclipse.org/uml2/5.0.0/UML/Profile/Standard'
)/]

[import ucmism2t::templates::query::oldModelQuery/]

[**
Returns an ordered set of direct sub datatypes of a datatype,
sorted by datatype name.
---
AQL operations used:
  eInverse(uml::Generalization) - Finds all Generalization elements that
                                  cross-reference aDataType; requires all
																	resources to be loaded in the same
																	resource set. Returns both generalizations
																	where aDataType is the general end AND
																	where aDataType is the specific end —
																	hence the guard below is mandatory.
  ->select(g1 | g1.general      - Retains only Generalization elements where
              = aDataType)        aDataType is the general (parent) end,
                                  excluding generalizations where aDataType
                                  is the specific (child) end. Without this
                                  guard, aDataType itself leaks into the
                                  result via .specific on its own supertype
                                  relationships.
  ->collect(g2 | g2.specific)   - Retrieves the specific (child) classifier
                                  of each qualifying Generalization element.
  ->filter(uml::DataType)       - Retains only uml::DataType instances,
                                  excluding non-DataType specializations and
                                  dropping null values safely.
  ->sortedBy(c | c.name)        - Sorts result alphabetically by datatype
                                  name.

@param aDataType - A UML datatype whose direct sub datatypes
                   are to be retrieved.
/]
[query public u_subDataTypes(aDataType : uml::DataType) : OrderedSet(uml::DataType) =
  aDataType.eInverse(uml::Generalization)
	  ->select(g1 | g1.general = aDataType)
	  ->collect(g2 | g2.specific)
	  ->filter(uml::DataType)
	  ->sortedBy(c | c.name)
/]

[**
Returns an ordered set of all sub datatypes of a datatype,
traversing the full specialization hierarchy down to the leaves.
Supports both single and multiple inheritance. Cycle-safe.
---
AQL operations used:
  ->closure(c | expr)    - Applied to aDataType itself as seed; the lambda
                           c.u_subDataTypes() is evaluated starting from
                           aDataType, so direct sub datatypes are included
                           from the first step. Traverses transitively until
                           no new elements are found. Cycle-safe: each element
                           is visited at most once. Returns
                           OrderedSet(uml::DataType) — no cast required.
  ->sortedBy(c | c.name) - Sorts the full result alphabetically by datatype
                           name.

@param aDataType - A UML datatype whose full sub datatype hierarchy
                   is to be retrieved.
/]
[query public u_allSubDataTypes(aDataType : uml::DataType) : OrderedSet(uml::DataType) =
  aDataType->closure(c | c.u_subDataTypes())
  	->sortedBy(c | c.name)
/]

[**
Returns an ordered set of classes which use the specified data type,
sorted by class name. Navigates the inverse usage links from
the data type, selects only those whose owner is a class,
collects and casts the owning classes, and deduplicates.

@param aDataType - A UML data type whose using classes are
                   to be retrieved.
/]
[query public u_usingClasses(
  aDataType : uml::DataType) : OrderedSet(uml::Class) =
  aDataType.u_usingProperties()
    ->select(p | p.owner.oclIsKindOf(uml::Class))
    ->collect(p | p.owner.oclAsType(uml::Class))
    ->asOrderedSet()
    ->sortedBy(c | c.name)
/]

[**
Returns an ordered set of data types which use the specified data type,
sorted by data type name. Navigates the inverse usage links from
the data type, selects only those whose owner is a data type,
collects and casts the owning data types, and deduplicates.

@param aDataType - A UML data type whose using data types are
                   to be retrieved.
/]
[query public u_usingDataTypes(
  aDataType : uml::DataType) : OrderedSet(uml::DataType) =
  aDataType.u_usingProperties()
    ->select(p | p.owner.oclIsKindOf(uml::DataType))
    ->collect(p | p.owner.oclAsType(uml::DataType))
    ->asOrderedSet()
    ->sortedBy(d | d.name)
/]

[**
Returns an ordered set of properties (attributes) that use the
specified data type, excluding association ends and properties
owned by the data type itself, sorted by the owning classifier name.

@param aDataType - A UML data type whose using properties are
                   to be retrieved.
/]
[query public u_usingProperties(
  aDataType : uml::DataType) : OrderedSet(uml::Property) =
  aDataType.eInverse(uml::Property)
    ->select(p | p.association = null)
    ->select(p | p.owner <> aDataType)
    ->sortedBy(p | p.owner.oclAsType(uml::Classifier).name)
/]

[**
Returns an ordered set of client data types of all abstraction
dependencies that target the specified data type, sorted by name.
Navigates inverse abstraction links from the data type, collects
their clients, and retains only data type instances.

@param aDataType - A UML data type whose abstraction clients are
                   to be retrieved.
/]
[query public u_abstractionClientsDataType(
  aDataType : uml::DataType) : OrderedSet(uml::DataType) =
  aDataType.eInverse(uml::Abstraction)
    ->collect(a | a.client)
    ->filter(uml::DataType)
    ->asOrderedSet()
    ->sortedBy(c | c.name)
/]

[**
Returns an ordered set of supplier data types of all abstraction
dependencies that target the specified data type, sorted by name.
Navigates inverse abstraction links from the data type, collects
their suppliers, and retains only data type instances.

@param aDataType - A UML data type whose abstraction suppliers are
                   to be retrieved.
/]
[query public u_abstractionSuppliersDataType(
  aDataType : uml::DataType) : OrderedSet(uml::DataType) =
  aDataType.eInverse(uml::Abstraction)
    ->collect(a | a.supplier)
    ->filter(uml::DataType)
    ->asOrderedSet()
    ->sortedBy(c | c.name)
/]

[**
Returns a sequence of owned attributes of the specified data type,
sorted by attribute name. Excludes association ends, retaining
only plain attributes owned directly by the data type.
Applies to all subtypes of uml::DataType, including
uml::Enumeration and uml::PrimitiveType.
Note: See the overloaded variants for classes and classifiers:
u_attributes(uml::Class), u_attributes(uml::Classifier).

@param aDataType - A UML data type whose owned attributes are to
                   be retrieved.
/]
[query public u_attributes(
  aDataType : uml::DataType) : Sequence(uml::Property) =
  aDataType.ownedAttribute
    ->select(p | p.association = null)
    ->sortedBy(p | p.name)
/]

[**
Returns an ordered set of all super datatypes of a datatype,
traversing the full generalization hierarchy up to the root.
Supports both single and multiple inheritance. Cycle-safe.
---
AQL operations used:
  ->closure(c | expr)    - Applied to aDataType itself as seed; the lambda
                           c.general->filter(uml::DataType) is evaluated
                           starting from aDataType, so the direct parent is
                           included from the first step. Traverses
                           transitively until no new elements are found.
                           Cycle-safe: each element is visited at most once.

@param aDataType - A UML datatype whose full supertype hierarchy
                   is to be retrieved.
/]
[query public u_superDataTypes(aDataType : uml::DataType) : OrderedSet(uml::DataType) =
  aDataType->closure(c | c.general->filter(uml::DataType))
/]

[**
Returns true if the specified data type is a general (parent)
data type, i.e. it has at least one specializing sub data type.

@param aDataType - A UML data type to check.
/]
[query public u_isGeneralDataType(
  aDataType : uml::DataType) : Boolean =
  aDataType.eInverse(uml::Generalization)
  ->select(g | g.general = aDataType)
  ->notEmpty()
/]

[**
Returns an ordered set of properties whose type is the specified
data type. Excludes association ends and properties owned by
the data type itself, i.e. returns only attributes of other
classifiers that reference this data type.

@param aDataType - The data type to find usages of.
/]
[query public u_dataTypeUseProperties(
		aDataType : uml::DataType) : OrderedSet(uml::Property) =
	aDataType.eInverse(uml::Property)
		->select(p |
			p.association = null
			and p.owner <> aDataType)
/]

[**
Returns a sequence of inherited attributes of the specified data type.
Excludes own attributes.

@param aDataType - A UML data type whose inherited attributes are to
                   be retrieved.
/]
[query public u_inheritedDataTypeAttributes(
  aDataType : uml::DataType) : Sequence(uml::Property) =
  aDataType.inheritedMember
    ->filter(uml::Property)
    ->select(p1 | p1.association->isEmpty())
    ->sortedBy(p2 | p2.name)
/]

[**
Returns an ordered set of packages of the context classifiers
of the specified data type, excluding the data type's own package,
sorted by package name.
See also: u_contextPackages(uml::Class)

@param aDataType - A UML data type.
/]
[query public u_contextPackages(
  aDataType : uml::DataType) : OrderedSet(uml::Package) =
  aDataType.e_contextClassesOrDataTypes()
    ->collect(c | c.package)
    ->excluding(aDataType.package)
    ->asOrderedSet()
    ->sortedBy(p | p.name)
/]

[**
Returns at most the first 3 properties that use the specified data
type, to keep diagrams manageable.

@param aDataType - A UML data type.
/]
[query public u_limitedDataTypeUseProperties(
  aDataType : uml::DataType) : OrderedSet(uml::Property) =
  let props : OrderedSet(uml::Property) =
    aDataType.u_dataTypeUseProperties()
  in
  if props->size() > 3 then
    props->subOrderedSet(1, 3)
  else
    props
  endif
/]
